TITLE:: SequencerGui
SUMMARY:: Provides a GUI to visually represent sequences created using a Sequencer.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Arranger, Classes/DrumProgrammer, Classes/Metronome, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollContainer, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter, Classes/SynthDesk, Classes/Tabset

DESCRIPTION::
LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: provides a visualisation of a graph of LINK::Classes/Pattern::s created using a LINK::Classes/Sequencer::. This is created when calling LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-showGui::. It owns a LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: wrapping LINK::Classes/Document#*current::, and a LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: whose active context is set when the user switches between Arrange, Record, and Settings views. The header bar includes Settings, Arrange, Record, Synths, and Drums buttons (Drums sits between Synths and the MIDI indicator). The Arrange button shows an embedded LINK::Classes/Arranger:: (the first page of the stack). Double-clicking one of its sequence labels loop-plays that sequence; double-clicking the playing label stops playback. TELETYPE::SequencerGui:: subscribes to the LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: with CODE::addDependant:: and forwards each CODE::\midiSequenceAdded:: id to LINK::Classes/Arranger#-addSequence::. The same subscription forwards CODE::\tempo:: to the embedded LINK::Classes/SynthDesk::. Closing the window removes that dependant and stops playback and recording on every piano roll so the shared clock can be released. The Settings view includes a tempo knob, which sets LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-tempo:: for the shared playback clock, and a knob for LINK::Classes/Metronome:: volume. The Synths button shows an embedded LINK::Classes/SynthDesk:: (the fourth page of the stack, after Arrange, Record, and Settings). The Drums button shows an embedded LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: (the fifth page). The record page is a LINK::Classes/PianoRollContainer::. Every roll, including the first, is named Sequence plus an incrementing count, starting at 1. The first roll is created by calling the tabset's LINK::Classes/Tabset#-addViewFunc::, and the CODE::+:: tab uses that same function. Only the selected roll receives record-context keystrokes and recording MIDI. Switching tabs is refused while that roll is recording. Any number of rolls can play loops at the same time. Start recording is on each roll. Play loop and Sync to are shown only when that roll is not recording and contains at least one note. Play loop snaps the piano-roll playhead onto that grid on the shared clock and starts immediately.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of LINK::Classes/SequencerGui::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that this LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: provides a visual representation of.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When CODE::true::, the embedded LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: skips MIDI setup and fills fake notes for development.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: update
Receives LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: notifications. CODE::\midiSequenceAdded:: adds that sequence name to the LINK::Classes/Arranger::. CODE::\tempo:: forwards the new tempo to the embedded LINK::Classes/SynthDesk::.

ARGUMENT:: theChanged
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that changed.

ARGUMENT:: what
The notification symbol. CODE::\midiSequenceAdded:: and CODE::\tempo:: are handled.

ARGUMENT:: id
The sequence LINK::Classes/Symbol:: when CODE::what:: is CODE::\midiSequenceAdded::. The new tempo when CODE::what:: is CODE::\tempo::.

PRIVATE:: init
